,"w":"800"},{"s":"congrats"}]},"codeShots":true,"why":"A deep pit of sea water in section, the nearest thing the kit has to the sea, with a toy submarine that floats, floods its ballast tanks to dive, blows them with compressed air to rise, cracks deep down and gets a thick hull. The camera stays on the submarine in mid shots, closes in on the tanks and the crack, and ends wide with the submarine at the surface.","hold":true},"sentences":[{"role":"hook","text":"If you seal a steel tube and drop it in the sea, you have a submarine."},{"role":"problem","text":"But it floats and bobs on the surface."},{"role":"fix1","text":"So you add tanks that flood with sea water, and it sinks."},{"role":"problem2","text":"But now it keeps sinking until it sits stuck on the bottom."},{"role":"fix2","text":"So you add tanks of air that blow the water out, and it rises."},{"role":"name","text":"This is a ballast tank."},{"role":"how","text":"Flood the tanks to dive, and blow them to rise."},{"role":"problem3","text":"But now deep down, the pressure squeezes the hull until it cracks."},{"role":"fix3","text":"So you wrap it in a thick hull of strong steel."},{"role":"fact","text":"Navy attack submarines dive deeper than 800 feet, and the exact depth is secret."},{"role":"finish","text":"Add a periscope and a propeller."},{"role":"congrats","text":"Congratulations, you have built a submarine."}]}